WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.033 --> 00:00:02.200
-I'm so happy to see you all.

00:00:02.200 --> 00:00:03.400
Thank you so much
for coming back to the show.

00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:05.334
And I'm so happy to see you.
-Yeah, finally.

00:00:05.334 --> 00:00:06.767
[ Laughter ]
[ Cheers ]

00:00:06.767 --> 00:00:10.300
-Last time -- Last time you were
on the show, you were sick.

00:00:10.300 --> 00:00:11.801
-I was.
-Yeah.

00:00:11.801 --> 00:00:13.734
And I'm so happy to see
you're not sick anymore.

00:00:13.734 --> 00:00:16.067
And I filled in.
I filled in for you.

00:00:16.067 --> 00:00:19.667
I was in the band for
three minutes, four minutes.

00:00:19.667 --> 00:00:22.067
[ Laughter ]
[ Cheers ]

00:00:22.067 --> 00:00:23.801
-You looked very good
with a blonde wig, though.

00:00:23.801 --> 00:00:25.100
-Thank you very much.

00:00:25.100 --> 00:00:27.000
Did you bring that blonde wig,
or did we find one?

00:00:27.000 --> 00:00:28.868
-No, no, now it's my turn.
Please, Jimmy.

00:00:28.868 --> 00:00:30.267
[ Laughter ]

00:00:30.267 --> 00:00:31.400
-No, no, no.
It's you.

00:00:31.400 --> 00:00:34.434
But here's me performing
with Maneskin

00:00:34.434 --> 00:00:35.901
last time they were on the show.
-Nice.

00:00:35.901 --> 00:00:37.567
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:37.567 --> 00:00:40.267
-I'm a bit jealous.
-Sorry, darling.

00:00:40.267 --> 00:00:42.400
You really can't see
the difference.

00:00:42.400 --> 00:00:44.701
-You can't tell the difference
at all, yeah, yeah.

00:00:44.701 --> 00:00:46.767
How did you rate --
did you see the performance?

00:00:46.767 --> 00:00:48.467
-Yeah, I saw it.

00:00:48.467 --> 00:00:49.634
[ Laughter ]

00:00:49.634 --> 00:00:51.067
-Okay.
Let's just leave it at that.

00:00:51.067 --> 00:00:52.667
-I don't know.
You were hot, though.

00:00:52.667 --> 00:00:54.133
You were hot.
-I was hot.

00:00:54.133 --> 00:00:56.801
-I was a bit jealous.
-You know what made me laugh?

00:00:56.801 --> 00:00:58.267
This is how much
your band loves you.

00:00:58.267 --> 00:01:00.901
They brought around
a cardboard cutout of you

00:01:00.901 --> 00:01:03.133
because you were sick.
No, for real.

00:01:03.133 --> 00:01:05.367
And we were posing
with pictures with you.

00:01:05.367 --> 00:01:07.801
You were here when you didn't
even know you were here.

00:01:07.801 --> 00:01:13.667
-I look excited, though.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:13.667 --> 00:01:15.467
-It was an honor to play
with you guys

00:01:15.467 --> 00:01:17.234
and to try
to step in your shoes.

00:01:17.234 --> 00:01:19.234
I tried.
I couldn't even hold a candle.

00:01:19.234 --> 00:01:22.133
I can't hold a candle to you.
Come on, you guys rock.

00:01:22.133 --> 00:01:26.834
Congratulations on getting
nominated for a Grammy

00:01:26.834 --> 00:01:28.868
for Best New Artist!
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:28.868 --> 00:01:30.367
Yes!
-Yes!

00:01:30.367 --> 00:01:34.400
-Maneskin, Best New Artist,
now Grammy-nominated!

00:01:34.400 --> 00:01:35.934
-Ah, yes.
-Forever.

00:01:35.934 --> 00:01:37.934
Forever you can say that.
-Yeah.

00:01:37.934 --> 00:01:39.834
-Where were you
when you heard the news?

00:01:39.834 --> 00:01:41.267
Did you freak out?
Were you excited?

00:01:41.267 --> 00:01:43.467
-Yeah, no.
We were in L.A.

00:01:43.467 --> 00:01:45.234
We were writing
the album, actually.

00:01:45.234 --> 00:01:48.868
-Yeah.
-And -- No, we were touring.

00:01:48.868 --> 00:01:51.234
-I don't know.
-I don't remember.

00:01:51.234 --> 00:01:54.067
It was early --
-Who -- Who heard it first?

00:01:54.067 --> 00:01:57.834
-I was, 'cause I'm, like,
the early bird of the band.

00:01:57.834 --> 00:02:01.067
[ Laughter ]

00:02:01.067 --> 00:02:05.434
And it streamed in the morning,
so I was the only one, like,

00:02:05.434 --> 00:02:07.267
really awake
in front of the television.

00:02:07.267 --> 00:02:10.801
They were all waking up
and getting dressed and stuff.

00:02:10.801 --> 00:02:13.501
And when they said our name,
I started screaming.

00:02:13.501 --> 00:02:17.200
And we were actually
shooting a video for this

00:02:17.200 --> 00:02:19.734
because we wanted, like,
to share the reaction,

00:02:19.734 --> 00:02:22.901
but we couldn't because it was
too vulgar, too aggressive.

00:02:22.901 --> 00:02:24.234
[ Laughter ]

00:02:24.234 --> 00:02:27.067
-Yeah, I heard him, like,
started banging on my door.

00:02:27.067 --> 00:02:28.801
Ooh.
And I was like, "Okay.

00:02:28.801 --> 00:02:30.200
What's wrong?
What have I done?

00:02:30.200 --> 00:02:31.634
I'm [bleep]."
-They all thought --

00:02:31.634 --> 00:02:33.968
They all thought
we didn't get the nom.

00:02:33.968 --> 00:02:36.701
-I thought just you wanted
to kill me or something.

00:02:36.701 --> 00:02:37.934
I was like,
"What did I do wrong?"

00:02:37.934 --> 00:02:39.033
-You thought he wanted
to kill you?

00:02:39.033 --> 00:02:40.200
-I was like, "Aah!",
locking the door.

00:02:40.200 --> 00:02:41.667
-You're locking the door,
like, "Stop, stop!"

00:02:41.667 --> 00:02:44.033
You were just so excited,
just yelling out curse words

00:02:44.033 --> 00:02:45.634
and screaming?
-Exactly.

00:02:45.634 --> 00:02:48.033
-Yeah, that's fantastic.
Well, congratulations.

00:02:48.033 --> 00:02:50.634
This is a big deal.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:50.634 --> 00:02:52.868
No matter what happens,
you're always Grammy-nominated.

00:02:52.868 --> 00:02:55.634
That's it.
No matter what happens.

00:02:55.634 --> 00:02:58.834
Also, another cool thing,
if you can get cooler

00:02:58.834 --> 00:03:00.267
than getting nominated
for a Grammy,

00:03:00.267 --> 00:03:03.100
but Mick Jagger chose you
to open for the Rolling Stones

00:03:03.100 --> 00:03:05.367
in Las Vegas.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:05.367 --> 00:03:09.200
He chose you.
He's like, "I want this band.

00:03:09.200 --> 00:03:10.968
I want this band."

00:03:10.968 --> 00:03:14.234
What was it like when you get
that call from Mick Jagger?

00:03:14.234 --> 00:03:15.834
You're like --
-"Whatever."

00:03:15.834 --> 00:03:16.968
[ Laughter ]
-Yeah, yeah.

00:03:16.968 --> 00:03:18.801
-"Maybe we can't do it."
-Just another day.

00:03:18.801 --> 00:03:19.901
-Just another day.

00:03:19.901 --> 00:03:21.033
-Just another day
in the music business.

00:03:21.033 --> 00:03:22.834
-Where was it?
Was it a stadium?

00:03:22.834 --> 00:03:24.901
-It was in Vegas, yeah.
Yeah, it was like our biggest --

00:03:24.901 --> 00:03:27.200
like, our first stadium,
so it was crazy.

00:03:27.200 --> 00:03:29.100
And, also, it was iconic
'cause we got the chance

00:03:29.100 --> 00:03:31.400
to talk to him,
and he was, like, so nice

00:03:31.400 --> 00:03:33.834
and knew a lot
of our music and stuff.

00:03:33.834 --> 00:03:36.634
And then, we met Keith Richards,
and he was like,

00:03:36.634 --> 00:03:38.334
"I don't know
who the [bleep] you are,

00:03:38.334 --> 00:03:40.267
but they told me you're good,
so..."

00:03:40.267 --> 00:03:41.634
We were like, "Okay."

00:03:41.634 --> 00:03:45.501
-"But you play real instruments,
so keep going."

00:03:45.501 --> 00:03:47.634
-"You play real instruments."
-And then he vanished.

00:03:47.634 --> 00:03:49.968
-And then he -- that's what
Keith Richards does.

00:03:49.968 --> 00:03:53.667
He says nice and iconic things,
then he vanishes.

00:03:53.667 --> 00:03:55.767
I want to talk about
the new album, "Rush."

00:03:55.767 --> 00:03:57.300
[ Cheers and applause ]
Congratulations.

00:03:57.300 --> 00:03:59.934
It's out.

00:03:59.934 --> 00:04:02.767
Can you explain
the cover of the album?

00:04:02.767 --> 00:04:04.033
-[ Laughs ]
-Well...

00:04:04.033 --> 00:04:05.801
-Sure.
-It's behind the meaning.

00:04:05.801 --> 00:04:07.968
-Yeah.
That's half of the meaning.

00:04:07.968 --> 00:04:10.200
-The meaning is behind.
-We cannot show you that.

00:04:10.200 --> 00:04:11.968
[ Laughter ]

00:04:11.968 --> 00:04:13.200
-You can imagine it, though.

00:04:13.200 --> 00:04:15.067
-But there's a girl
jumping over you guys.

00:04:15.067 --> 00:04:16.467
-Yeah.

00:04:16.467 --> 00:04:19.334
-And what I like is the
expression on your faces.

00:04:19.334 --> 00:04:21.434
Can we just zoom in just to --
[ Laughter ]

00:04:21.434 --> 00:04:22.901
Everyone's got
a different expression.

00:04:22.901 --> 00:04:24.400
-Yeah.
Yeah.

00:04:24.400 --> 00:04:26.601
-Is that kind of expressing
what you guys

00:04:26.601 --> 00:04:28.067
are going through right now?
-Exactly.

00:04:28.067 --> 00:04:29.267
-Kind of.
-More or less.

00:04:29.267 --> 00:04:31.234
-Good guess.
-Yeah, it was like, we tried to

00:04:31.234 --> 00:04:33.434
represent the whole year
we've been through

00:04:33.434 --> 00:04:36.601
and all of the different moods
we had and how each one coped,

00:04:36.601 --> 00:04:38.601
like, with the stress
and everything, also.

00:04:38.601 --> 00:04:40.601
And it's represented, like,
as something cool

00:04:40.601 --> 00:04:43.567
'cause she's jumping
and we can see under her skirt.

00:04:43.567 --> 00:04:45.000
[ Cheers ]
-Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:04:45.000 --> 00:04:47.167
-But also as something that
could fall over you, you know?

00:04:47.167 --> 00:04:49.200
So it's like this double thing.
-Yeah.

00:04:49.200 --> 00:04:53.033
I mean, it feels like
you've been around.

00:04:53.033 --> 00:04:54.300
But it's all new.

00:04:54.300 --> 00:04:55.934
I mean, you're new artists
and all.

00:04:55.934 --> 00:04:59.234
But every time you perform,
you crush, I will say.

00:04:59.234 --> 00:05:00.367
I'm a fan.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:00.367 --> 00:05:01.667
Every time I've seen you.

00:05:01.667 --> 00:05:03.334
And it's nerve-wracking.
I go, "Oh.

00:05:03.334 --> 00:05:05.934
Are they gonna do it again?"
And you do it again.

00:05:05.934 --> 00:05:07.934
And you do it again.
And you do it again.

00:05:07.934 --> 00:05:09.267
And I love
that you keep doing it.

00:05:09.267 --> 00:05:11.601
So, congratulations to you.

00:05:11.601 --> 00:05:12.667
You're doing something tonight.

00:05:12.667 --> 00:05:14.334
What are you
playing tonight for us?

00:05:14.334 --> 00:05:16.100
-Once again, "Beggin'" --
No.

00:05:16.100 --> 00:05:17.701
[ Laughter ]

00:05:17.701 --> 00:05:19.000
I'm joking.
-"Gossip"!

00:05:19.000 --> 00:05:20.901
-We're playing "Gossip" with --
-Finally.

00:05:20.901 --> 00:05:23.501
-With Tom Morello.
-With a special guest.

00:05:23.501 --> 00:05:26.000
-With a special guest.
With Tom Morello.

00:05:26.000 --> 00:05:27.300
-The legend.
-Come on.

00:05:27.300 --> 00:05:29.567
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:29.567 --> 00:05:32.033
How does it go?
Do you get excited when you get

00:05:32.033 --> 00:05:33.634
to play with Tom Morello when --

00:05:33.634 --> 00:05:34.801
You know,
I have a photo here of --

00:05:34.801 --> 00:05:37.334
You guys started
busking in Rome.

00:05:37.334 --> 00:05:39.501
That's how you got your start.
This is you guys --

00:05:39.501 --> 00:05:40.701
[ Cheers ]

00:05:40.701 --> 00:05:42.033
What was a --

00:05:42.033 --> 00:05:45.734
What is a big day for you guys
at busking, moneywise?

00:05:45.734 --> 00:05:48.234
-A good day meant like...
-50?

00:05:48.234 --> 00:05:50.467
-...between 20 and 50 euros.

00:05:50.467 --> 00:05:54.033
But the most important thing
was going back home with zero

00:05:54.033 --> 00:05:56.801
[bleep] offs from
the pedestrians.

00:05:56.801 --> 00:05:57.968
-Oh, 'cause people
would scream that at you.

00:05:57.968 --> 00:05:59.901
-Which happened rarely,
honestly.

00:05:59.901 --> 00:06:02.367
-Yeah, that was very hard
not to get insulted.

00:06:02.367 --> 00:06:03.567
-Usually you would get insulted

00:06:03.567 --> 00:06:05.334
by at least one or two people
per day?

00:06:05.334 --> 00:06:06.834
-Even more, even more.
-At least.

00:06:06.834 --> 00:06:08.934
-At least?
And what would you --

00:06:08.934 --> 00:06:11.067
Would you play covers
or just originals?

00:06:11.067 --> 00:06:13.601
-Mostly covers.
We had, like, two originals.

00:06:13.601 --> 00:06:14.834
-Also, yeah,
and some were our songs.

00:06:14.834 --> 00:06:17.467
-Two originals.
-And would the cops just

00:06:17.467 --> 00:06:18.834
break you up and go,
"Get out of there"?

00:06:18.834 --> 00:06:21.200
-Very often. We would be like,
"Oh, my God, I'm sorry.

00:06:21.200 --> 00:06:23.267
We didn't know that,"
and then like wait five minutes

00:06:23.267 --> 00:06:25.901
hidden and then --
-Do it again.

00:06:25.901 --> 00:06:27.968
-We were like, "Oh, my God.
We didn't know that."

00:06:27.968 --> 00:06:30.868
-That's what's it's --
it's called, drive, everybody.

00:06:30.868 --> 00:06:32.367
That's what it's called.

00:06:32.367 --> 00:06:33.801
You've got it.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:33.801 --> 00:06:35.934
I'm so happy you're here.
Thank you so much.

00:06:35.934 --> 00:06:38.367
You look great in person.
I'm so happy to see you guys.

00:06:38.367 --> 00:06:39.934
Maneskin, everybody!

00:06:39.934 --> 00:06:41.033
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:41.033 --> 00:06:44.100
Their new album, "Rush,"
is available now!

00:06:44.100 --> 00:06:46.400
Number one, by the way,
in over 20 countries.

00:06:46.400 --> 00:06:47.767
Congrats on that, too.

00:06:47.767 --> 00:06:50.434
They're performing with
Tom Morello when we come back!

00:06:50.434 --> 00:06:51.968
Stick around!

